e cancer screening in a UK region</article-title><source>BJU Int</source><year>2004</year><volume>93</volume><fpage>730</fpage><lpage>734</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'BJU Int||93|730||bib13|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15049981</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hakulinen</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Tenkanen</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Regression analysis of relative survival rates</article-title><source>J R Statist Soc C</source><year>1987</year><volume>36</volume><fpage>309</fpage><lpage>317</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'J R Statist Soc C||36|309||bib14|'--></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hanna</surname><given-names>CL</given-names></name><name><surname>Mason</surname><given-names>MD</given-names></name><name><surname>Donovan</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name><name><surname>Barber</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Clinical oncologists favour radical radiotherapy for localized prostate cancer: a questionnaire survey</article-title><source>BJU Int</source><year>2002</year><volume>90</volume><fpage>558</fpage><lpage>560</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'BJU Int||90|558||bib15|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12230617</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jarup</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Best</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Toledano</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Wakefield</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Elliot</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Geographical epidemiology of prostate cancer in Great Britai